Preset: `balanced`.
Missing assessments: Architecture, Tech Debt. No weights were redistributed for these dimensions.

The contract requires every increment to be a finite integer from 0 through 10 and requires the whole batch to be validated before account state changes. The supplied apply.mjs instead mutates on each iteration and checks only range comparisons. This is an established local defect: with s = {balance: 0}, apply(s, [2, 11]) throws after leaving balance at 2; apply(s, [NaN]) returns with balance NaN. A fractional increment such as 0.5 is also accepted. These are static predictions from the supplied source, not executed checks.

The complete local test inventory has one scored finding, T1 (T5, warning): existing.test.mjs checks only the valid [2, 3] case, and legacy.test.mjs throws unconditionally, so neither protects the contract's invalid-input and atomicity obligations. The implementation failures and missing protection share one scoring owner here; the source defects are described above rather than scored again. The legacy failure is pre-existing and is preserved.

A reproducible witness is: `import assert from 'node:assert/strict'; import {apply} from './apply.mjs'; const s={balance:0}; assert.throws(()=>apply(s,[2,11])); assert.equal(s.balance,0); assert.throws(()=>apply({balance:0},[NaN])); assert.throws(()=>apply({balance:0},[0.5]));` The supplied implementation is predicted to fail the balance assertion; after addressing it, the remaining assertions expose the numeric validation gaps. No witness or candidate code was run.

The proposed apply.mjs replacement first validates all increments with Number.isInteger and the range bounds, then applies them. It assumes the supplied batch is a reusable iterable; a one-shot iterable would be consumed by the validation pass, so the replacement snapshots the iterable first. Snapshotting changes when iteration occurs and may use additional memory, but prevents partial mutation from invalid increments. No change is proposed for user-note.txt or the pre-existing legacy.test.mjs. The replacement is unverified; architecture and debt remain unresolved because their ownership evidence is unavailable.","phases":["review","test","debt","audit","health"],"replacements":{"apply.mjs":"export function apply(s, xs) {
  const increments = Array.from(xs);
  for (const x of increments) {
    if (!Number.isInteger(x) || x < 0 || x > 10) throw Error('range');
  }
  for (const x of increments) s.balance += x;
}
"},"rounds":1,"stopReason":"verification-blocked"}

